---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/support-pages.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Meet Ron Walker | HVAC Training Solutions"
  description="Meet Ron Walker, the instructor behind HVAC Training Solutions and HVAC Boot Camp. Learn how his field and management experience shapes the training."
>
  <div class="support-page about-page">
    <section class="support-hero about-hero">
      <div class="support-shell about-hero-inner">
        <p class="support-eyebrow">Meet your instructor</p>
        <h1>Good training makes the work make sense.</h1>
        <p class="support-lead">Ron Walker brings field and management experience into online HVAC training, helping learners connect what they study with the way a technician thinks through a system.</p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/try-boot-camp/">Watch Ron teach</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="support-section" aria-labelledby="about-ron-title">
      <div class="support-shell about-story">
        <div>
          <p class="support-eyebrow">Ron Walker</p>
          <h2 id="about-ron-title">Experience from the field, brought into the lesson.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="about-prose">
          <p>After retiring from the U.S. Marines and earning a bachelor’s degree, Ron entered HVAC. His work has included roles as a technician, service manager, and business owner.</p>
          <p>Those different views of the trade shape the way he teaches: learn the fundamentals, understand what a system is doing, and practice explaining your reasoning. A quiz answer alone is not the same as understanding the work.</p>
          <p>Online study can help you build that foundation. Field skills still require supervised practice with an employer or qualified professional.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="support-shell about-experience" aria-label="Ron's background">
        <div><strong>HVAC technician</strong><span>Hands-on experience with equipment and service work</span></div>
        <div><strong>Service manager</strong><span>A view of how technicians learn and solve problems</span></div>
        <div><strong>Business owner</strong><span>Experience with the expectations around the job</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="support-section support-section-soft">
      <div class="support-shell about-approach">
        <div class="support-heading">
          <p class="support-eyebrow">The teaching approach</p>
          <h2>Make one idea click, then build on it.</h2>
          <p>In HVAC Boot Camp, Ron uses textbook reading, video lessons, and quizzes to build an understanding of the systems behind the work.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-principles">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>Explain the “why”</h3><p>Connect pressure, heat, airflow, and electrical ideas to what happens in equipment.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>Check understanding</h3><p>Work through a focused question and learn from the feedback.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>Prepare for real work</h3><p>Use the knowledge to ask better questions and enter supervised training with a foundation.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="support-section support-last">
      <div class="support-shell support-next-step">
        <div><p class="support-eyebrow">Start with a free lesson</p><h2>See how Ron teaches before you decide.</h2><p>Watch his public refrigeration cycle lesson, then review the full Boot Camp curriculum and course format.</p></div>
        <div class="support-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/try-boot-camp/">Watch the lesson</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/hvac-boot-camp/">Explore Boot Camp</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
